00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:03.480
Today I have a friend challenging me

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.760
to take a popular food and...

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.020
make it fancy.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.984
Today's guest is-

00:00:08.984 --> 00:00:10.350
(hands thumping)

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.220
- It's me.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.053
- Elise!

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:16.020
- I am so excited for you
to see what I brought today.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.922
- I'm a little scared.
- It's gonna be amazing.

00:00:17.922 --> 00:00:19.980
- Okay.
- It's gonna be amazing.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.323
- All right, let's see what
we are making fancy today.

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:26.220
- Ta-da!
- Panda Express.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.620
Is this orange chicken?

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.453
- [Elise] Yes.

00:00:29.453 --> 00:00:30.900
- I love orange chicken.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.390
- Orange chicken is like a staple.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.733
And I think it would be an
interesting challenge for you

00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:37.740
to, you know, make it fancy.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.540
- Well, you know, just a refresher.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.770
Let's try.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:41.823
- [Both] Cheers.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.153
- Crunchy.

00:00:44.153 --> 00:00:45.510
- Saucy.
- Tangy.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:49.680
- Well, you know, actually I
have an additional challenge

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.540
on top of what I've already given you.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.740
I want you to make this
Panda Express orange chicken

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.740
into like a breakfast hangover cure.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.939
- Breakfast hangover cure.

00:01:00.939 --> 00:01:02.130
- Mm-hmm.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.020
That's my challenge for you.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:05.550
- Challenge accepted.

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:06.383
- Woo.

00:01:06.383 --> 00:01:08.070
- All right, I'm excited to-

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:09.690
- Make it fancy.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.190
- All right, here's what I got.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.023
Eggs.

00:01:12.023 --> 00:01:13.140
Asparagus.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:13.973
Dill.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:14.806
Chives.

00:01:14.806 --> 00:01:15.639
Lemons.

00:01:15.639 --> 00:01:16.472
Grapefruit.

00:01:16.472 --> 00:01:17.305
Shallots.

00:01:17.305 --> 00:01:18.138
Ground chicken.

00:01:18.138 --> 00:01:18.971
Arugula.

00:01:18.971 --> 00:01:19.804
Milk, butter.

00:01:19.804 --> 00:01:22.860
And Panda Express orange sauce.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:26.760
By the way, you can buy this
merch at www.shop.buzzfeed.com.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.620
From the pantry I got-

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.453
Olive oil.

00:01:29.453 --> 00:01:30.300
Canola oil.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.200
Rice vinegar.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.040
White vinegar.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.150
Dijon mustard.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.140
Maple syrup

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:34.973
Honey.

00:01:34.973 --> 00:01:35.806
Semolina flour.

00:01:35.806 --> 00:01:37.410
Panko breadcrumbs.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.610
Instant yeast.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:39.870
Red pepper flakes.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:40.800
Brown sugar.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.210
Ground allspice.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.170
Cayenne pepper

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.360
And smoked paprika.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.910
All right, let's get started.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:49.260
Making it fancy.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:50.610
So first step,

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:55.050
I have box a full of Panda
Express orange chicken.

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.790
I'm gonna do little surgery.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:57.720
Looks so good.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.240
I want to separate
chicken from the breading.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.530
Something about this orange
chicken I crave once in a while.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:07.860
So I separated all chicken and breading

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:12.360
and I'm going to chop
the chicken super fine.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.620
And I'm super excited what I'm
going to do with this later.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.640
Looks good.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.680
So I'm going to save this for later

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.570
and I'm going to spread
this in two portions.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.090
I think orange chicken tastes so good

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.030
because it hits all the flavor.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.940
Salt, fat, acid, and sweetness.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.260
All right, looks good.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.410
And I'm going to put
this in the dehydrator

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:39.150
until it become crispy.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.920
While it's dehydrating,

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.147
let's get fancy.

00:02:42.147 --> 00:02:44.980
(classical music)

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:01.170
This is came out from the
dehydrate and it's so crispy.

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:03.360
I'm gonna try small piece.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.350
It's like meat candy.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.090
Sorry, you guys cannot taste it.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:08.850
I'm going to put this in a spice grinder

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:11.310
and make it into coarse powder.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:15.870
All right, now I have orange
chicken flavored powder.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:17.880
I can't wait for you to see

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.400
how I'm going to use this magical powder.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.900
All right, so since Elise
challenged me to make breakfast,

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.300
I've decided to do some baking.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.240
What's better than fresh
baked goods in the morning?

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.520
I have half cup of water.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.350
And warm milk, half cup.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:36.000
And sugar.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.790
Whisk a little bit so sugar dissolve.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.620
I'm going to bloom yeast.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:44.220
When you are using rapid
yeast, you want to activate.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:47.400
So you want to use warm water or milk.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.480
It's important so you are making
sure the yeast is not dead.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.660
I'm going to set aside
about 5 to 10 minutes

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:55.680
until it's foaming.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.440
All right, I have all purpose flour

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:02.820
and I have powdered chicken
breading and adding salt.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:07.440
I'm gonna combine, mix dry
ingredients well with whisk.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:08.940
I have two eggs.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:10.620
This is the bloomed yeast.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.385
And I'm going to add-

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:13.380
Ah!

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:15.630
I'm going to add eggs.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.580
and melted butter.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:18.540
Whisk.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:23.540
And I'm going to add dry
ingredients and wet mixture slowly.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:27.420
And I'm going to mix it with dough hook

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.700
until the dough is very elastic.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.140
Sprinkle.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:34.380
You want to knead the dough until elastic.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:37.170
You need dough to create gluten.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.710
So this dough supposed
to be sticky like this.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.460
So I think it's ready.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.580
And I'm going to put in a glass bowl.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:48.330
And we are going to proof
this dough until doubled.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.480
So I have proof the dough.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:52.650
It is double in size.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.810
Gonna dust on my surface.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.520
Dust my rolling pin, too.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.350
So it produced gas.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.840
I kind of want to be gentle on it

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.344
so I don't want to deflate.

00:05:03.344 --> 00:05:05.280
Whoa, look at this.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.820
I want to roll this about a inch.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.610
I'm going to cut this.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:12.840
One down.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:15.150
And when you are cutting and rolling,

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.610
make sure to dust your utensils.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:21.120
Like, dust your rolling pin
and dust your ring mold.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.680
Look, my baby.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:26.850
I have sheet pan with semolina flour on it

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:30.840
so it doesn't stick and gives
a nice kind of texture, too.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:33.720
My orange chicken batter
bread dough is ready

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.830
and let's cook them off.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:38.820
I have semolina flour and I'm
going to sprinkle in the pan.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.920
And we are not using any cooking oil.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:44.310
So I'm going to cook
all the semolina flour.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:47.700
About five minutes until
the bottom is golden brown.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.790
One of the indicator since
we are using semolina,

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:54.090
you can see semolina is getting
brown, maybe it's ready.

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:55.440
Let's see.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:56.273
Slippery.

00:05:56.273 --> 00:05:57.420
Oh, nice.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:01.320
And I'm going to cook the other
side about five more minutes

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:04.950
and I'm going to cook off
rest of the English muffins.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:06.780
So those look great.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:10.740
And we are going to finish
this in the oven at 350,

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:12.060
about five minutes.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:13.470
But most important part,

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:16.380
it's inner temperature is 180 degree.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:19.290
So this is new element of my dish

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:22.260
and I brought back chopped
chicken right here.

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:23.730
Ground chicken.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.220
And chopped chicken.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:31.220
And I have maple syrup,
cayenne pepper, smoked paprika.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:36.590
Brown sugar, ground allspice,
salt and black pepper.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.050
I'm going to mix this.

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:42.330
The best kitchen tool, my hand.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:47.330
And I'm going to divide
this into six even sides.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.370
Make sure everything is kind of even.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:51.203
Cool.

00:06:51.203 --> 00:06:54.600
I took out sausage from the
freezer and it's chilled.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:57.150
The reason we chill this in the freezer

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.460
so it doesn't stick on the bottom.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:01.503
And I'm going to add oil.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:07.950
And put the ring mold so we
can have nice round shape.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:09.420
Take out this.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:11.040
Chill the sausage ball.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:14.280
Cook until brown and all cook through.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:15.690
I have four more to go.

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:19.080
And I'm gonna finish this and
we are moving on to next step.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.650
So I have eggs and I'm going to separate.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:25.080
I think this is just a practice.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:28.410
Just go back and forth
and gently remove white.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:32.190
So I have egg yolk and orange sauce.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:35.730
Lemon juice, salt and cayenne pepper.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:37.770
When you make hollandaise sauce,

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.720
you usually use double-boiler.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.940
But this is a tasty hack.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.410
You can use blender.

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:46.440
And I'm going to start the blender

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.750
and heat it up about 20 seconds.

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:52.350
And then slowly add melted, warm butter.

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:56.070
You want to blend egg
yolk first to heat it up.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:59.460
So egg yolk and butter
temperature is the same

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:01.290
so the sauce won't be separated.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:04.560
This was so much faster
and easier using blender

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:05.610
than the double-boiler.

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:08.430
My hollandaise sauce looks delicious.

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:10.650
And we are moving on to next step.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:13.920
I want to add some freshness into my dish.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:15.990
So I'm going to make a little salad.

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:18.540
I have rice vinegar.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:19.800
Lemon juice.

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.510
So I'm adding orange sauce

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:24.450
because Elise loves orange chicken.

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:25.503
Honey.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:27.900
Chili pepper flake.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:30.150
And salt is to taste.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.740
Dijon mustard.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:33.090
And olive oil.

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:34.860
And I'm gonna use immersion blender

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:38.040
so it is easy and faster to emulsify.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:42.330
I'm gonna add minced
shallot and lemon zest.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.180
I think it is very vibrant, fresh.

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:47.400
And there is a hint of orange sauce.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.290
All right, salad is ready.

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:50.190
Let's move on.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:52.230
We have boiling hot water

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:55.260
and I'm going to salt and white vinegar.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:59.010
The reason I put vinegar
is hold the shape better

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.020
and I'm going to crack egg

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:06.000
and I'm going to create vortex
and I'm going to drop egg.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.340
Look at this, like dancing.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:11.250
Be very careful not to break the yolk.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:16.230
The visual cue is inside
it's still jiggly.

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:19.530
And egg white is kind of coated around it.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:23.460
And another important thing is
you don't want to boil water.

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:25.260
You want to make it simmer.

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:27.570
It's like outside is completely cooked

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:30.420
but inside you can kind of see runny yolk.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:34.200
So I made poached egg, but this is not it.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:37.920
I'm going to freeze this and elevate this.

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:42.270
I have dehydrated and ground
orangey chicken breading.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:44.280
I'm going to mix with panko.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:46.170
First, I'm gonna coat.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:47.130
This is not frozen.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:50.010
It's chilled, still delicate.

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:51.390
So be gentle.

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:52.860
Egg wash.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:56.400
My hack when you are breading something,

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.950
use one hand for egg wash

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.200
so the other hand is not dirty.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.300
All right, so I have hot oil here

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:05.520
and I'm going to fry them.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:10.520
Just wanted to make outside
crispy, not fully-cooked inside.

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:15.620
One thing I think I'm surprised
is here in United States,

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:19.320
people eat greasy food as a hangover cure.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:23.700
When I get hangover I usually
want to eat something light.

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:28.230
Rice porridge like
congee, or miso soup even.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:32.370
So I feel like each country
has a different hangover cure.

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:34.710
All right, I think it's good to go.

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:35.640
Let's recap.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:39.840
I have dehydrated ground
orange chicken breading,

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:40.710
english muffin,

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:43.500
breakfast sausage with
chopped orange chicken,

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:46.830
the hollandaise sauce
with the orange sauce,

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:49.500
dressing with the orange sauce,

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:52.560
dehydrated ground orange
(record scratches)

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:56.340
chicken breading coated poached egg.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:00.570
And I have blanched
asparagus and chive and dill.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:05.100
Recently I learned you don't
want to cut English muffin

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:06.060
with knife.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:08.340
You want to use folk.

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:10.740
English muffin has nice kind of holes

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:13.860
so it doesn't destroy the holes.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:16.050
Just gently break.

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:17.010
Perfect.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:18.150
Let's assemble.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:21.573
Gonna put some salad, asparagus, sausage.

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:24.750
Fried poached egg.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.430
Hollandaise sauce.

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:28.410
Garnish with chives.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.913
And we are done.

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:34.230
(soft gentle music)

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:41.940
Panda Express orange
chicken eggs benedict.

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:42.810
Very fancy.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:45.900
Let's bring back our special guest, Elise.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:48.330
You challenged me.
- I did.

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:50.190
- Panda Express orange chicken.

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:52.050
And I made something for you.

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:52.883
- Here I go.

00:11:54.472 --> 00:11:56.772
(hands thumping softly)

00:11:56.772 --> 00:11:57.810
- What?

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:59.340
Eggs are my favorite food.

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:02.790
So seeing this here, is blowing my mind.

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:05.550
- Oh yay!
- It looks so beautiful.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:06.660
Life is just good right now.

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.010
Like, I'm so satisfied.

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:10.350
Is this eggs benedict?

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:11.183
- Better.

00:12:11.183 --> 00:12:13.140
- I would love to try it.
- Yes.

